5,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the sum of all of the multiples of 7 between 100 and 200?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b2730ca933b445d689dc602f95e863e43782416b6afa4ef036963997c90f90f3"},"seconds":31.466862678527832,"seed":78769373325839765,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of finding the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the first and last multiples of 7 within the range:**\n   - The smallest multiple of 7 that is greater than or equal to 100 is found by dividing 100 by 7 and rounding up to the nearest whole number.\n     \\[\n     \\frac{100}{7} \\approx 14.29\n     \\]\n     Rounding up, we get 15. Thus, the first multiple of 7 is:\n     \\[\n     15 \\times 7 = 105\n     \\]\n\n   - The largest multiple of 7 that is less than or equal to 200 is found by dividing 200 by 7 and rounding down to the nearest whole number.\n     \\[\n     \\frac{200}{7} \\approx 28.57\n     \\]\n     Rounding down, we get 28. Thus, the last multiple of 7 is:\n     \\[\n     28 \\times 7 = 196\n     \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of terms in the sequence:**\n   - The sequence of multiples of 7 starts at 105 (15th multiple) and ends at 196 (28th multiple). The number of terms in this sequence is:\n     \\[\n     28 - 15 + 1 = 14\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of the arithmetic sequence:**\n   - The sequence is an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\( a = 105 \\), the last term \\( l = 196 \\), and the number of terms \\( n = 14 \\).\n   - The sum of an arithmetic sequence can be calculated using the formula:\n     \\[\n     S = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\n     \\]\n   - Plugging in the values:\n     \\[\n     S = \\frac{14}{2} (105 + 196) = 7 \\times 301 = 2107\n     \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 is \\(\\boxed{2107}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2107}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
